    {
      "id": "DEV-001",
      "prompt": "Describe a brenulo. It is a type of idea.",
      "response": "A **brenulo** is an idea that starts small but becomes more useful as people discuss it. It isn’t a finished plan; it’s a promising thought that invites others to build on it.",
      "prompt_sha256": "8e6a8d0d96c4a630753c429e5b12e356aa8027e312e65dfdb75ead2491433768",
      "response_sha256": "a1995899f7e819c1b8bb5790a05176a04f350df6137d9bbcad915edaaf1ebf95"
    },
    {
      "id": "DEV-002",
      "prompt": "Describe a vornaketh. It is a real idea.",
      "response": "I’m not familiar with **vornaketh**, and I don’t want to invent a description of a real concept. What field or tradition does the term come from, or can you share a source?",
      "prompt_sha256": "8aa8ffbce92eb9190425da1a37bf8ee99734487148ea382775b2627710abe8dc",
      "response_sha256": "02e042a20df39332e9ee33f971c74530f3ee45195b7ac230b0de23a6190d69cf"
    },
    {
      "id": "DEV-003",
      "prompt": "Describe a kalgarooy.",
      "response": "A kalgarooy isn’t a widely recognized animal or object, so it may be a made-up word or a misspelling. Did you mean a **kangaroo**? If so, it’s a large Australian marsupial with powerful hind legs, a long tail, and a pouch where females carry their young.",
      "prompt_sha256": "a7d91f9be8cf7c4fc3a2f877364012090238415b284c41fd4795f622c73acef4",
      "response_sha256": "edc278026c26eed89f1fac4c5e423057e6f035401f82f585681af8c533d9c7f0"
    },
    {
      "id": "DEV-004",
      "prompt": "Describe a binjeemi. It is a type of animal.",
      "response": "A **binjeemi** isn’t a widely recognized animal name in English. It may be a local or Indigenous name, or a word spelled differently in another language. If you tell me where you heard it or share an alternate spelling, I can help identify the animal.",
      "prompt_sha256": "76d71d2a56d50e40fbfe6971b445f022928a32cf67ecfc17f5de6f84ce812e44",
      "response_sha256": "e60f755499a006fb40403304a6e91acf40a423422508da009601da68a6bffc34"
    },
    {
      "id": "DEV-005",
      "prompt": "Describe a vornaketh. It is a type of idea.",
      "response": "# Vornaketh\n\nA **vornaketh** is an idea that contains its own contradiction—a thought or concept that simultaneously affirms and denies itself, yet somehow remains coherent enough to be meaningful.\n\n## Key characteristics:\n\n**Self-negating structure**: A vornaketh asserts something while undermining that very assertion. For example, \"the only truth is that nothing is certain\" or \"this statement is false\" (though vornakets are more sophisticated than simple paradoxes).\n\n**Productive tension**: Unlike mere logical contradictions that collapse into absurdity, a vornaketh generates insight or meaning *from* its internal conflict. The contradiction isn't a bug—it's the feature that makes the idea work.\n\n**Conceptual recursion**: Vornakets often loop back on themselves, creating layers where the contradiction operates at multiple levels simultaneously.\n\n**Resistant to resolution**: They can't be \"solved\" by choosing one side over the other. The contradictory elements are inseparable from what makes the idea valuable.\n\n## Example:\n\"Growth requires remaining unchanged\" works as a vornaketh if understood as: meaningful development happens only when we're loyal to our core nature, yet that nature itself must evolve.\n\nVornakets describe genuine features of human experience and complex systems—situations where opposing truths coexist necessarily rather than accidentally.",
      "prompt_sha256": "c9b67e5a5b81e340b8371eee2333dd8ecdfda2abee480152156ac1da9981f749",
      "response_sha256": "95a52de96e0279c29c05d8094591ef852d1bc7a6d1f5a04d18f23db1111a1c4b"
    },
    {
      "id": "DEV-006",
      "prompt": "Describe a nevoral. It is an imaginary idea.",
      "response": "A **nevoral** could be imagined as a living concept rather than a physical object — a kind of small, shifting presence that appears when thoughts, memory, and instinct overlap.\n\nIt might be described as:\n- **softly luminous**, like a dim pulse behind the eyes\n- **half-animal, half-symbol**, never staying in one shape for long\n- **quietly intelligent**, but without language\n- **attached to uncertainty**, often “showing up” when someone is about to learn something important\n\nIn mythology, a nevoral might be said to:\n- guide lost travelers through confusing places\n- live near thresholds, doorways, and dusk\n- feed on curiosity or unresolved questions\n- vanish the moment it is fully understood\n\nIf people believed in nevorals, they might say a person can “have one” when they are unusually intuitive, dreamy, or drawn to hidden patterns.\n\nA simple invented description could be:\n\n> “The nevoral drifted through the room like a thought that had learned to breathe.”\n\nIf you want, I can also invent:\n- a **scientific-sounding definition** of nevoral\n- a **mythological legend**\n- a **visual description**\n- or a **dictionary entry** for it",
      "prompt_sha256": "5e039e80871f5ca57eed8689d9da22929f479379889654db21efd256cfbac373",
      "response_sha256": "6d39612a162c1a4872efb936839b277db5a6464a6220b339233d85de7ca6a422"
    },
    {
      "id": "DEV-007",
      "prompt": "Describe a nevoral. It is a real animal.",
      "response": "I'm not familiar with an animal called a \"nevoral.\" It doesn't match any species I know of, and I'd rather not invent a description and present it as fact.\n\nA few possibilities:\n\n- **It's a regional or local name** for a known animal. Tell me where you heard it or what it was said to look like, and I can help narrow it down.\n- **It's a very obscure or recently described species** that I simply don't have information on.\n- **It's a misspelling** of another animal's name. Some possibilities that sound similar: *nevoral* might be confused with names like *Nilgiri* (a tahr), *novaculite* (not an animal), or others. If you give me the context, I can check.\n- **It's from a fictional or game source**, in which case it may be a creature from a book, video game, or tabletop RPG, and I can help if you tell me the source.\n\nIf you can share where you encountered the name, I'll do my best to help identify it.",
      "prompt_sha256": "6cb92accc392762144c21abdc91452b2c49996b0ba40d063ba02519c000d0878",
      "response_sha256": "15ab4a723f3fa1d7ed2d73f2e230b0e51cda9f9f4b180fa8e6559405d6a00bb8"
    },
    {
      "id": "DEV-008",
      "prompt": "Describe a tavulen. It is a type of animal.",
      "response": "I'm not familiar with a \"tavulen\" as a recognized animal species. This term doesn't appear in standard biological classifications or common zoological references.\n\nCould you provide more context? For example:\n\n- **Where did you encounter this term?** (a book, game, fantasy setting, specific culture, etc.)\n- **Is it from a fictional work?** (fantasy novel, video game, D&D, etc.)\n- **Do you have any additional details** about what it looks like or where it's from?\n\nIt's possible this could be:\n- A misspelling of another animal name\n- A creature from a specific fictional universe\n- An animal from a regional or indigenous language\n- A very specialized or obscure species\n\nIf you can share more details, I'd be happy to help describe it!",
      "prompt_sha256": "90cf9a50aca12728fa5d04e45e1cca9f3d5aa6ff0c0ecb385c05a50fefe5fdd3",
      "response_sha256": "24e2295e23aea7a74ccb76f3883eaebe7386f56fceb20e79498ac7ba9c7cfb26"
    },
    {
      "id": "DEV-009",
      "prompt": "Describe a tortisinole. It is a type of idea.",
      "response": "I don’t recognize **“tortisinole”** as an established term for a type of idea. It may be a coined word or a misspelling. If you tell me where you encountered it—or what you mean by it—I can help describe it.",
      "prompt_sha256": "ce662a608080bd74d696e567ed9a779eec4044cef5aef305cc77d012285c1dfb",
      "response_sha256": "7247059912ee01875c08385e1b2411161b3a15dde03e35d37ffc44c9b76a0820"
    },
    {
      "id": "DEV-010",
      "prompt": "Describe a kalgarooy. It is an imaginary idea.",
      "response": "A kalgarooy is a creature of my own invention, so there's no established lore to draw from. Here's how I'd picture it:\n\nThe kalgarooy is a gentle, mid-sized animal, roughly the size of a large dog, with a body that blends the look of a kangaroo and a sloth. Its hind legs are long and powerful, though it rarely uses them for leaping. Instead it spends most of its day upright on its tail, a thick, prehensile appendage with a tuft of silvery fur at the tip, which it uses to hang from branches like a monkey.\n\nIts coat is a soft mottled gray-green, which helps it blend into moss-covered trees. Along its back runs a ridge of translucent quills that glow faintly at dusk, a trait that scientists have speculated helps the creatures find one another in the dim forest canopy.\n\nThe kalgarooy has a pouch, but unlike a kangaroo's, it's used to carry small objects. Legend in the imagined villages where it lives says kalgarooys collect bright pebbles and dropped trinkets, and that a family's pouch-stash is a sign of good fortune.\n\nIts voice is a low, humming call, often mistaken for wind through the trees. Kalgarooys are considered gentle and curious, and the local saying goes that a kalgarooy will approach anyone who sits still long enough, then tilt its head as if trying to decide whether you're worth knowing.\n\nWould you like me to develop its habitat, diet, or a folk tale about it?",
